  <article class="project-story">
    <figure class="project-story-visual project-story-visual-bookxcess">
      <div><img src="/assets/images/work/bookxcess-case.webp" alt="BookXcess Online ecommerce storefront" width="1088" height="1252" loading="lazy" decoding="async"></div>
      <figcaption>BookXcess Online · Work completed with the Upstack Studio team</figcaption>
    </figure>
    <div class="project-story-copy">
      <p class="page-kicker">Ecommerce · BookXcess</p>
      <h3>Fixing the immediate commercial bottleneck.</h3>
      <p>When pandemic restrictions stopped physical retail and book events, BookXcess had to rely on its online store. The existing Shopify experience was slow, difficult to use and carrying problems that needed urgent attention.</p>
      <dl>
        <div><dt>What we changed</dt><dd>We focused on the customer experience, site performance and the design problems standing between shoppers and a purchase.</dd></div>
        <div><dt>What I took forward</dt><dd>Urgency sharpens prioritisation. Fix the constraint affecting customers and revenue before expanding the scope.</dd></div>
      </dl>
      <a class="text-link" href="https://clutch.co/go-to-review/1e4ccebe-2c58-45fe-8b6a-a22a8d81dd5f/201640">Read Dinie Johari’s project review on Clutch{{ icon("external", "link-arrow") }}</a>
    </div>
  </article>

  <article class="project-story">
    <figure class="project-story-visual project-story-visual-teleme">
      <div><img src="/assets/images/work/teleme-case.webp" alt="Teleme patient and healthcare practitioner app screens" width="1270" height="1204" loading="lazy" decoding="async"></div>
      <figcaption>Teleme · Work completed with the Upstack Studio team</figcaption>
    </figure>
    <div class="project-story-copy">
      <p class="page-kicker">Healthcare · Teleme</p>
      <h3>Making a complex service easier to use.</h3>
      <p>Teleme was building a digital healthcare ecosystem connecting patients, doctors and pharmacies. We helped turn that service into mobile experiences for both patients and healthcare practitioners.</p>
      <dl>
        <div><dt>The product challenge</dt><dd>Different users needed to find care, communicate and complete important actions without being overwhelmed by the system behind them.</dd></div>
        <div><dt>What I took forward</dt><dd>Complex products become useful when each person can understand the next step. The technology should make that action feel simple.</dd></div>
      </dl>
      <blockquote><p>“The end product is not only good but better than what we have expected.”</p><cite>Kevin Ong · Former CTO, Teleme</cite></blockquote>
      <a class="text-link" href="https://clutch.co/go-to-review/1e4ccebe-2c58-45fe-8b6a-a22a8d81dd5f/39537">Read the Teleme project review on Clutch{{ icon("external", "link-arrow") }}</a>
